{"id":"n6919917a4e","headline":"Aussie inflation print justifies RBA rate hike","summary":"The ABS released August quarter consumer price inflation a day after the Reserve Bank of Australia raised the official cash rate by 0.25%. The RBA said inflation remains elevated.","why":"The Reserve Bank of Australia sets the country's cash rate, which influences borrowing costs, the Australian dollar and asset prices. Consumer price inflation is its key gauge when setting policy.","category":"economy","event_type":"rates","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Sydney","country":"Australia","lat":-33.87,"lon":151.21,"region":"oc"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"MacroBusiness","url":"https://www.macrobusiness.com.au/2026/09/aussie-inflation-print-justifies-rba-rate-hike/"},"sources":[{"name":"MacroBusiness","url":"https://www.macrobusiness.com.au/2026/09/aussie-inflation-print-justifies-rba-rate-hike/"}],"published_at":"2026-09-30T01:44:17Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-12T08:33:11Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"c2415e709cb1581f","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-12T08:33:11Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-09-30T01:44:17Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-09-30T03:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"AS","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/central-bank-building-4352072.jpg","alt":"central bank building (illustration)","credit":"Leonhard_Niederwimmer","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/new-york-usa-nyc-ny-manhattan-4352072/"}}